    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core led by **Yordan Alvarez** (78.05) and **Junior Caminero** (76.17). **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier offensive engine, boasting an elite 0.461 xwOBA against Ure\u00f1a, while **Junior Caminero** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Scherzer\u2019s 5.08 xERA. **Trea Turner** (73.73) rounds out our top trio; he is an essential start given his elite sprint speed and a positive BvP historical edge against Alcantara. We are also leaning heavily on **Caleb Durbin** (64.41), whose projection is buoyed by Pfaadt\u2019s slow delivery, creating an optimal environment for **Caleb Durbin** to capitalize on his elite base-stealing profile in a category where we remain hyper-aggressive.\n\nOur lineup construction required a difficult cut regarding **Josh Smith** (38.83), who fell just shy of our 40-point floor threshold. While **Josh Smith** possessed a strong dynamic platoon advantage, the combination of a tough matchup against Rasmussen and a sub-optimal batting order position necessitated his benching in favor of higher-floor contributors. We must also exercise caution with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (53.28); while his speed is a vital asset, he is facing a left-handed starter, resulting in a significant 15% penalty to his output. Similarly, **Colt Keith** (45.44) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (39.24) face uphill battles against high-skill arms in Skenes and Rasmussen, respectively. The heavy SP skill penalties for those matchups underscore the importance of maintaining our discipline, as we prioritize efficiency to manage our remaining game caps for the stretch run.",
